+# Edge Worker Session Validation
+
+## Overview
+
+Sessions are now signed with RS256 (RSA SHA-256) so the edge worker can validate them without database access.
+
+## Key Setup
+
+Generate an RSA key pair (origin service only):
+
+```bash
+openssl genrsa -out private.pem 2048
+openssl pkcs8 -topk8 -inform PEM -outform PEM -in private.pem -out private_key.pem -nocrypt
+openssl rsa -in private_key.pem -pubout -out public_key.pem
+```
+
+Set environment variables:
+
+**Origin service** (`DATABASE_URL` is required):
+```bash
+SESSION_PRIVATE_KEY="$(cat private_key.pem)"
+DATABASE_URL="postgres://..."
+```
+
+**Edge worker** (no database, no private key):
+```bash
+SESSION_PUBLIC_KEY="$(cat public_key.pem)"
+```
+
+## How It Works
+
+### Issuance (Origin Service)
+
+When creating a session:
+```ts
+const token = signSession(sessionId, userId, expiresAt);
+// Returns a JWT that's valid for `expiresAt` minutes
+```
+
+### Validation (Edge Worker)
+
+The edge worker validates the token:
+```ts
+const session = await loadSession(token);
+if (!session) {
+  // Token is invalid, expired, or signature doesn't match
+  return 401;
+}
+// Token is valid, use session.userId
+```
+
+No database call. No network roundtrip. Signature verification is instant.
+
+## Revocation Trade-off
+
+**Revocation on the origin**: `revokeSession(id)` still marks sessions as revoked in the database. This prevents access at the origin.
+
+**Revocation at the edge**: Cannot revoke immediately. The edge worker will continue accepting valid tokens until they expire (by design, since it has no way to check the database).
+
+**Mitigation**: Use short session lifetimes (e.g., 15-60 minutes) so revoked sessions expire quickly.
+
+## Architecture
+
+```
+Origin Service:
+  - Has DATABASE_URL + SESSION_PRIVATE_KEY
+  - Issues signed tokens via signSession()
+  - Can revoke tokens (marks in DB, prevents future issuance)
+  - Validates tokens locally (no DB call for validation)
+
+Edge Worker:
+  - Has SESSION_PUBLIC_KEY only
+  - Validates tokens by checking signature + expiry
+  - No database access at all
+  - No ability to revoke tokens (by necessity)
+```
